    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "One or two given names and a family name; since 2013 couples may keep their own names or share one. Swiss family names are tied to a place of origin (Heimatort) and often come from trades or farms (Müller, Meier, Keller, Brunner). Romansh names like Seraina, Ladina or Gian come from Graubünden and are popular across the country. Zurich has large Italian, German, Portuguese, Kosovo Albanian, Balkan and Turkish communities, who keep their own names.",
